// A module that declares its OWN ports, instead of taking the one audio input its type folder
// would have given it. That is the whole reason a crossfade was unsayable before: `audio/` means
// one in, one out, and a folder is not the right place to decide how many wires an effect takes.
//
// `mandatory: false` on `b`: wiring one side and leaving the other silent is a legitimate state,
// not a half-built chain. Drop this module into a chain on its own and it plays deck A alone.
//
// `plugin: {type: jsdsp}` says the sound comes from the `jsdsp.ts` beside this file — one
// statement for both facts, so there is no `dsp:` field to keep in step with a plugin name.
plugin({ type: "jsdsp", name: "Crossfade" })
inputs([name("a").type("audio"), name("b").type("audio").mandatory(false)])
outputs([name("out").type("audio")])
params({
  // The graph's own parameter, by its display name — that is how a param finds its plugin
  // (see applyPluginParams). Centred: both decks at once, which is what makes the demo audible.
  Mix: 0.5,
})
// A two-input crossfade. Mix at 0 is deck A alone, at 1 deck B alone, at 0.5 both at half.
// (Was `docs:`. To say this on the GRAPH, wire this module into a node of `@meta/doc`.)
